 "triage": {
  "summary_md": "## Duplicate purchases are charged twice on NewSwitch v1\n\n**Severity:** critical · **Rule:** Reject a duplicate purchase (same card, STAN and amount within 60 seconds)\n\nThe new switch approves a retried purchase that the legacy switch rejects with **94 Duplicate transmission**.\nBoth legacy copies (Old A and Old B) agree, so this is not noise.\n\n| Retry gap | Old A | Old B | New |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 s | 94 | 94 | 94 |\n| 0.5 s | 94 | 94 | 94 |\n| 1 s | 94 | 94 | **00** |\n| 5 s | 94 | 94 | **00** |\n| 59 s | 94 | 94 | **00** |\n| 61 s | 00 | 00 | 00 |\n\n### Boundary\n- Retries **1 second or more** apart are approved and debited a second time.\n- Retries inside the same second are still caught.\n- After 60 seconds both switches agree (new purchase).\n\n### Root-cause hypothesis\nThe 60-second duplicate window appears to be read as **60 milliseconds** (`dup_window` unit mismatch).\n\n### Money at risk\nIn the 2,000 replayed transactions, 41 regressions totaling `$6,874.12` would have been double-charged.\n\n_Data is IBM TabFormer (public synthetic benchmark). The defect was seeded for this demo._\n",
